# <Feature Name> — Walkthrough Narration

One `>` block per shot. The TTS toolkit turns each block into a per-shot audio
clip (hash-cached) and lays it over the recording at the shot's REAL start time:

```bash
<venv-python> platform/tts/generate.py --dir walkthroughs/<p>/modules/<m>/features/<f>
<venv-python> platform/tts/build_narrated.py --dir walkthroughs/<p>/modules/<m>/features/<f>
```

**Voice:** warm, confident, product-demo. Business language only — what the
user sees and achieves, never implementation.

> **Prefer generating this file.** When the feature has a `feature.yaml`, this
> file is rendered from its `narration:` fields by
> `node platform/scripts/generate-feature.mjs <feature-path>` — edit the yaml,
> not this file. Hand-author only for quick experiments outside the catalog.
>
> **Timings are captured automatically.** The spec's `timer.mark(N)` writes each
> shot's real start to `generated/shot-timings.json`; clips are placed there —
> no hand-measured timecodes.
>
> **Shot headings must match.** `generate.py` maps each `## Shot N` heading's
> `>` block onto shot N. Keep numbers aligned with the spec / feature.yaml.
>
> **Skipped guarded shots** never appear in `shot-timings.json`; their clips are
> dropped automatically at mux time.
>
> **If a clip outruns its shot window:** default `--mode extend` freezes the
> shot's last frame to make room (no overlap); `--mode exact` keeps video length
> (may overlap); `--mode sequential` plays clips back-to-back and stretches.

